#! btw 1
#! name: vocals
#! license: CC0-1.0
#! visibility: public
# vocals: lyrics that read like code (CC0-1.0, an original track). docs/btw/phonemes.md
# Plain words go through the BeatScript lexicon; text between slashes is phonemes, sung exactly as written
# (`aa:` holds a syllable over the next note, `ay!` accents it); `@id` is a phrase of the phrasebook.
# In the browser a sing line is part of its deck's net: it plays through the deck's fader and the crossfader.
tempo 124
key am

deck A: kick x ~ x ~ | hihat ~ x ~ x vel=60..90 | bass a2 a2 e2 g2
deck B: melody <[a4 c5 e5 c5] [g4 b4 d5 b4]>

section call 8 bars {
  deck B: sing "we are the rave to-night" on melody voice=robot-choir
}

section answer 8 bars {
  deck B: sing "/w ee - aa: r - dh uh - r ay! v/ _ /h ie - er/" on melody voice=robot
}

section hands 8 bars {
  deck B: sing @hands_up on melody voice=android
  # the voice on deck B shapes deck A's bass and hats, as an insert on A (its fader and the crossfader take it)
  do vocoder set carrier=A modulator=B insert=true on=true mix=0 -> 1 over 8 bars
}

section turn 8 bars {
  deck B: sing @feel_the_bass on melody voice=talkbox
  at bar 4: move vocoder_handoff on A
}

arrange call answer hands turn
